<title>FRANCE: TABLE-HERMES INTL FIRST-HALF SALES RISE.</title>
<headline>TABLE-HERMES INTL FIRST-HALF SALES RISE.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>     Turnover			     2,186  vs  1,914</p>
<p>	- includes Q2		     1,106  vs    970</p>
<p>Breakdown by sector</p>
<p>	- silks				 581  vs    584</p>
<p>	- leather goods		     506  vs    401</p>
<p>	- ready-to-wear fashion	   311  vs    246</p>
<p>- other (includes stationery,</p>
<p>	    hats, shoes, jewellery)     213  vs    153</p>
<p>	- perfume			     129  vs    144</p>
<p>	- watches/clocks		    216  vs    194</p>
<p>	- dining ware			  93  vs     88</p>
<p>- other (includes John Lobb</p>
<p>				 brand)	 137  vs    104</p>
<p>NOTE - Hermes International gave its first-half sales in the official bulletin BALO.</p>
<p>At constant exchange rates, the rise in sales was 11.6 percent over year-earlier levels. At constant exchange rates and structure, the rise was 9.1 percent, it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
